# Intentionally empty. Permanent redirects live in ONE place:
# src/data/redirects.json, which worker/index.ts imports.
#
# This file is Cloudflare's static-asset redirect layer. It stays empty and
# unused because a second redirect mechanism is a second place to look when a
# URL misbehaves, and only the worker's map is checked: check-parity fails a
# row that is not also in wrangler.jsonc run_worker_first, smoke-worker asserts
# every 301 locally, and smoke-live asserts the same rows against production.
# Nothing verifies a rule written here.
#
# What does not belong in EITHER place:
#  - trailing-slash normalisation — wrangler.jsonc html_handling does it
#  - www -> apex — a zone-level Redirect Rule (dashboard), because it fires
#    before the request reaches this worker's hostname at all
#  - /hi/<code> — a REWRITE (the URL must stay in the address bar), which
#    lives in worker/index.ts
